== Q2b identity check: alpha = Z0/(2 R_K) with R_K = h/e^2 (exact in the 2019 SI) and Z0 = 1/(eps0 c) ==
  R_K = 25812.8074593 ohm ; Z0 = 376.730313412 ohm ; Z0/(2 R_K) = 0.00729735256433 ; 1/(that) = 137.035999177 ; miss vs 137.035999177 = 2.18e-13 (limited by the 11 recalled digits of eps0)
  algebra: Z0/(2 R_K) = (mu0 c) e^2/(2 h) = e^2/(4 pi eps0 hbar c) = alpha exactly; so 'F = Z0/(Z0 + 2 R_K) = alpha + O(alpha^2)' equals alpha/(1+alpha) with 1/F = 138.035999177, miss 0.007297 relative (= alpha)

